# omdrcctrl-renderer — passwordless sudo for exactly the two renderer units'
# start/stop, plus mpd.service's, nothing else.  Needed because upmpdcli.service,
# qobuzconnect2mpd.service and mpd.service are systemd SYSTEM units with
# User=@AUDIO_USER@ (not systemd --user — see cmake/renderers.cmake and each
# unit's own header comment for why), so the things that manage them —
# omdrcctrl's web toggle and restart buttons and the omdrc-renderer boot
# restorer — all run as @AUDIO_USER@ and need root to start/stop a system unit.
# mpd.service is included because a wedged MPD (seen once: memory pressure
# from an unrelated restart storm left its accept() loop starved, with no
# crash and nothing for Restart= to react to) has no other recovery short of
# a manual `sudo systemctl restart mpd` — the Restart button on the MPD panel
# needs the same grant `renderer_restart` already has for the two renderers.
# This is the Linux equivalent of the FreeBSD rc.d NOPASSWD grant in
# omdrc-ctrl/README.md.
#
# Rendered by CMake (cmake/renderers.cmake) and staged under
# @PREFIX@/share/omdrc/sudoers.d/omdrcctrl-renderer, syntax-checked with
# `visudo -c` at install time — but NOT written into /etc/sudoers.d itself:
# like the udev rule / mpd drop-in / modprobe.d files, that directory is
# outside CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX and is host state a packaged or DESTDIR build
# must not touch. Copy it into place as part of the first-install checklist:
#
#	sudo cp @PREFIX@/share/omdrc/sudoers.d/omdrcctrl-renderer /etc/sudoers.d/
#	sudo chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/omdrcctrl-renderer
#	sudo visudo -c
#
@AUDIO_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start qobuzconnect2mpd.service, \
    /usr/bin/systemctl stop qobuzconnect2mpd.service, \
    /usr/bin/systemctl start upmpdcli.service, /usr/bin/systemctl stop upmpdcli.service, \
    /usr/bin/systemctl start mpd.service, /usr/bin/systemctl stop mpd.service
